  "notes": "USAGE:\nSense 1 (pity) is the most common modern usage. Sense 2 (feel pathos) is more literary and connected to the classical aesthetic of もののあわれ (mono no aware).\n\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし}), む-ending.\n- Negative: {哀|あわ}れまない\n- Polite: {哀|あわ}れみます\n- Te-form: {哀|あわ}れんで\n- Past: {哀|あわ}れんだ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{哀|あわ}れむ: to feel sorry for someone\n- {哀|あわ}れみの{目|め}: a pitying look\n- {哀|あわ}れみを{感|かん}じる: to feel pity",
